course: dictionary
lesson: 11780
title: Bedside words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bedside is made of two small words, bed and side. The side of a bed is the place next to it, so bedside means next to the bed. «The glass of water sat on the bedside table.» The clue is table: a small table that stands beside the bed.
explain: Bedside can also describe a person. «Dad sat at her bedside all night while she was poorly.» Ask yourself where the sitting happens. It is next to a bed, with a sick person lying in it, so being at someone's bedside means staying close to them while they are ill in bed.
explain: Context gives you the feeling too. «The doctor had a gentle, kind bedside manner and spoke softly to the children.» Gentle and kind are the clues. Bedside manner means how kindly a doctor or nurse talks to patients, not anything about the bed itself.
fact: Bedside means the area next to a bed.
fact: A bedside table or bedside lamp is one you keep next to the bed.
fact: Being at someone's bedside means staying with them while they are ill in bed.
fact: «Bedside manner» means how kindly a doctor talks to patients.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: «The lamp is on the table next to the bed» still makes sense.
exercise: «The glass of water was on the bedside table.» Where was the glass? | In the bath | Under the bed | On the kitchen floor | *Next to the bed
exercise: «Dad sat at her bedside all night while she was poorly.» What does at her bedside mean here? | Asleep on the stairs | Dancing in the kitchen | Sitting in the garden with her | *Sitting next to her while she is ill in bed
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means next to the bed: «Switch on the bedside lamp so I can read.» | read | lamp | *bedside | switch
test: «The doctor had a kind bedside manner, and she spoke softly to the children.» What does bedside manner mean? | How quickly a doctor can run | *How kindly a doctor talks to patients | The name of a hospital bed | How much a doctor likes to eat
test: Which meaning fits best in «a bedside lamp»? | A lamp made only of wood | *A lamp kept next to a bed | A lamp for the garden | A lamp stuck on the ceiling
exam: Which sentence uses bedside correctly? | «The dog bedside barked at the postman.» | «Let's bedside the lake for a swim after school.» | «The bedside is a fish that swims in the sea.» | *«Grandad put his glasses on the bedside table before he slept.»
